            <ArticleTitle>Awareness of and compliance with air pollution advisories: a comparison of parents of asthmatics with other parents.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>235-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVES" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To determine parents' awareness of and compliance with air pollution advisories, and to compare the awareness and compliance of parents' of asthmatics to that of other parents.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">Responses of 240 parents surveyed at pediatric clinic visits were compared.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">A total of 88% of parents were aware of air pollution advisories; 71% reduced pollution and 55% restricted children's play &quot;sometimes&quot; because of advisories. However, only 7% complied with more than one third of the advisories issued. More parents of asthmatics reported awareness of alerts (p = 0.002), reducing pollution (p = 0.005), or restricting play &quot;sometimes&quot; in response to advisories (p = 0.007).</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Most parents report awareness of and some compliance with air pollution advisories. Parents of asthmatics are more aware and somewhat more compliant than other parents.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
